WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.501 size:84% position:42%
-Welcome to the show.
-Well, thank you, Seth.

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.069
-I want to tick off some thing
that are impressive about you.

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're one of the most popular
governors in America,

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:07.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
you are a Republican in
a blue state,

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:09.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you have been
vocally critical

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:10.210 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
of the president.

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:14.080 line:92%
Why are there not more of you?

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:17.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
Well, that's a good question

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:19.919 size:84% position:42%
You know, I'm kind of
one in a million, Seth.

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:21.354 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I mean, you know...

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:24.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think that there probably ar
some other folks out there

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:27.660
that are like me, but they don't
get a lot of attention.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, look, like most people
in America,

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:34.768
I'm completely fed up with all
this divisive, angry politics,

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:37.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think that --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:42.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, so, I'm in a state that
has 26% Republican.

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:45.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just got overwhelmingly
re-elected as a Republican

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
70% of my legislature
is Democrats.

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:49.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I've worked toward
the middle

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:51.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
and tried to find
that common ground,

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:52.919 line:92%
where we can all stand together.

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:55.588
And I just happen to believe
that there's a whole lot mor

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.690 line:92%
that unites us than divides us

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:01.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we should do away
with all the angry politics.

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:03.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You are --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:06.933
You just became chair of the
National Governors Association

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:09.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a bipartisan group
of all our governors.

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:10.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm pretty sure that's
the first time

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:13.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
they've ever mentioned the
National Governors Association

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:14.474 line:92%
on late-night television.

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:17.811 line:92%
-Yeah. It has not come up, yeah.

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:19.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
You maybe noticed the slow way
I said it

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:20.847 line:92%
to make sure I got it right.

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:24.284
You are a part of a group called
the...National --

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:26.519
-National Governors Association.
-Yeah.

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:30.623
Tell me, though -- This does not
look like you're dancing with --

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:31.991 line:92%
That's -- Is that Marie Osmond

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:34.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That is Marie.
Yeah, it was last --

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:35.195 line:92%
-So, here, everybody thought

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:37.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, National Governors
Association --

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:37.897 line:92%
that sounds super-boring,"

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:38.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
but there you are
rockin' it out.

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:41.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, so, last Friday,
I just became the chairman

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they had
a little event afterwards.

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:44.604 line:92%
Donnie and Marie put on a show

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:46.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she dragged me up on
the stage and embarrassed me

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:50.410
And, look, I'm hoping I can ge
a Nutrisystem gig out of it.

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:53.279 line:92%
-Yeah, I was going to say.

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:58.585
You are a Republican who
believes in climate change

00:01:58.585 --> 00:02:00.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
You believe that's
a very serious issue.

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.522 line:92%
You also -- Which is great

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:04.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
You also believe
in infrastructure.

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:07.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you feel as though
infrastructure can lead to

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:09.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
helping eradicate
climate change?

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:12.332
I know, for example, you have --
in your state,

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:15.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
you have moved more money
towards highway infrastructure

00:02:15.335 --> 00:02:17.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
as opposed to
public transportation.

00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:18.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
That seems maybe
counterintuitive

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:20.540
to somebody who believes climate
change is such a big deal.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not really true,
but thanks for saying that

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:23.710 line:92%
-Which -- Well, there was a --

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:25.044
I mean, I don't want to get into
transportation.

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:29.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, we've invested $14 billio
in transit,

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.451 line:92%
about $9 billion in roads.

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:32.485 line:92%
We've just moved forward.

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:34.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're under construction
with the largest

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:37.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
public-private transit project
in North America.

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:40.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I pushed through tougher
clean-air standards

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:44.831
than 48 other states and twice
as strong as the Paris Accords

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:46.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
as a Republican governor
in Maryland.

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And do you feel as though
you are --

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:50.603 size:78% position:39%
And I genuinely think
that's great news.

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:52.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you feel as though you're
making progress

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:53.373 line:92%
with the other governors?

00:02:53.373 --> 00:02:56.376
Because it seems to me -- Yo
basically wrote an op-ed sayin

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:59.445
that, yes, federally, right now,
Donald Trump is moving awa

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:00.380 line:92%
from the Paris Climate Accords

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:03.216
but you believe, state by state,
this can be addressed.

00:03:03.216 --> 00:03:04.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Look, so we have
a group called RGGI,

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:07.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is the Regional
Greenhouse Gas Initiative.

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:08.688 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We had nine states.

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:12.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
We now have 13 states
on the East Coast

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:13.092 size:81% position:41% line:92%
that are all together.

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:14.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think we are
making a difference.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:17.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
Some states are taking it more
seriously than others,

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:18.498 line:92%
but my new role as chairman of

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:19.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
the National Governors
Association --

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:22.001
I'm representing Democrati
and Republican governors,

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:24.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I can tell you that people
are focused on the issue

00:03:24.904 --> 00:03:25.572 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and taking it seriously.

00:03:25.572 --> 00:03:28.641
And one of the great thing
about this organization is -

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:31.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's a really bipartisan,
nonpartisan group

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:34.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
on infrastructure,
which I just launched

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:35.215 size:88% position:44% line:92%
my initiative last week.

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:38.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's disagreement
among Republicans and Democrat

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:39.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
about how to
solve these problems,

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:42.555
but we're actually getting
things done in the states,

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:44.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
unlike Washington,
where it seems like we hav

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:48.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
nothing but divisiveness,
and dysfunction and gridlock

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:50.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
we're getting things done.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:50.997 size:88% position:44% line:92%
That's what people want.

00:03:50.997 --> 00:03:51.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Which is great,
and I'm really glad.

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:55.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, again, I think it is
the issue of this generation

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:59.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I'm really happy that
you are taking it seriously.

